{"id":"3881eb1aa39c55466554f300","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/24/australia-news-live-shark-attack-leah-stewart-housing-rents-first-home-cost-of-living-antisemitism-royal-commission-icac-politics-economy-sydney-melbourne-ntwnfb","published_at":"2026-08-24T01:37:46Z","collected_at":"2026-08-24T01:55:01.555384Z","title":"Australia news live: Joyce says One Nation MP got migration policy wrong; second fur seal dies of suspected bird flu","text":"19.25 EDT Joyce steps in on One Nation’s migration target Barnaby Joyce says a fellow One Nation MP made a mistake on Sunday by suggesting the minor party’s migration numbers would not be much different to Labor’s, AAP reports. One Nation MP David Farley told the ABC on Sunday that the party’s migration policy would include an extra 100,000 people annually, to provide a necessary regional workforce, on top of the 130,000 it had already flagged. Hanson forced to intervene after One Nation MP says party’s migration target ‘not too different’ from Labor’s Read more The overall number would be slightly higher than the forecast 225,000 people under Labor’s policy. The comments from Farley were soon corrected by party leader Pauline Hanson on social media, who said the policy remained to reduce net overseas migration to 130,000 people. Joyce said Farley had misspoken when he made the comments on migration numbers: Show me a political career where people haven’t made a mistake, and I’ll show you a person who’s not told the truth. I’m not going to throw anybody under a bus. When people are new in parliament, they can sometimes get things incorrect, and that’s what happens. God knows, I’ve ","html":"","media":[],"author":"Nick Visser","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"0a3c45074f13a0c7a5fb978be92376c0a168267d803916572afb8cdd6ae558a9","original_text_chars":1310,"original_html_chars":3360,"text_truncated":true,"media_count":0,"platform":{"entry_id":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/24/australia-news-live-shark-attack-leah-stewart-housing-rents-first-home-cost-of-living-antisemitism-royal-commission-icac-politics-economy-sydney-melbourne-ntwnfb","entry_link":"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/24/australia-news-live-shark-attack-leah-stewart-housing-rents-first-home-cost-of-living-antisemitism-royal-commission-icac-politics-economy-sydney-melbourne-ntwnfb"}}}
{"id":"5a79ae3d0464c16fcd83934f","source":"guardian-rss","source_name":"The Guardian World","platform":"rss","url":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/aug/24/trump-plans-critical-minerals-deep-sea-mining-pacific-islands","published_at":"2026-08-24T01:34:41Z","collected_at":"2026-08-24T01:55:20.000461Z","title":"US territories hit out at Trump plan to explore deep sea mining in the Pacific","text":"Leaders in the Northern Mariana Islands and Guam have expressed opposition to US plans to auction deep sea mining leases. Photograph: Amazing Aerial/Alamy View image in fullscreen Leaders in the Northern Mariana Islands and Guam have expressed opposition to US plans to auction deep sea mining leases. Photograph: Amazing Aerial/Alamy Deep-sea mining US territories hit out at Trump plan to explore deep sea mining in the Pacific US agency releases plan to lease millions of hectares of seabed off the coast of the Northern Mariana Islands and Guam Mar-Vic Cagurangan in Hagatna, Guam Sun 23 Aug 2026 21.34 EDT Last modified on Sun 23 Aug 2026 21.36 EDT Share Prefer the Guardian on Google A US government plan to lease out millions of hectares of seabed near the Mariana Trench for deep sea exploration has drawn opposition from US territories in the Pacific, as the Trump administration remains locked in a race with China for control of critical ocean minerals. On Tuesday, the Marine Mineral Administration (MMA), an agency under the US department of the interior, released a proposal to auction deep sea mining leases for 28m hectares (69m acres) of seafloor off the coast of the Northern Marian","html":"","media":["https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/6477bf1a810003e7b073c564f349c808c12a3a34/127_0_3749_3000/master/3749.jpg?width=465&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none","https://i.guim.co.uk/img/media/bbbc50af1dfb7c9b7daf0770f400563e856db028/0_0_3715_2477/master/3715.jpg?width=445&dpr=1&s=none&crop=none"],"author":"Mar-Vic Cagurangan in Hagatna, Guam","language":"und","group":"international-media","perspective":"mixed","trust":"high","tags":[],"raw":{"archive_policy":"public_excerpt_v1","content_sha256":"577c857d00b61c5a741ea54c77599a02c42aba2a8717d86dde8339ac632c71a9","original_text_chars":5034,"original_html_chars":20573,"text_truncated":true,"media_count":2,"platform":{"entry_id":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/aug/24/trump-plans-critical-minerals-deep-sea-mining-pacific-islands","entry_link":"https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/aug/24/trump-plans-critical-minerals-deep-sea-mining-pacific-islands"}}}
